{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966802,"nonce":"pZrqL2gjzNqZ9aLleqhx1aUFYw8=","title":"cn_demo's three spinners pinned ~60% CPU because rotation_timeline kept is_any_animating()","message":"`render_tree_with_motion_opt` decides whether to reuse `cached_texts` / `cached_svgs` / `cached_images` via an `any_motion_active` predicate. The original predicate ORed in `motion_bindings.values().any(b.is_any_animating())`, and `is_any_animating()` returns `true` whenever a `rotation_timeline` is playing.\n\ncn::spinner uses an infinite-loop `rotation_timeline` — so the flag stays true forever, the cache-hit path always fails, and the collect pipeline walks the entire element tree 60× per second to rebuild text/SVG/image vectors. With three spinners on screen, this pinned ~60 % CPU even though the spinners themselves don't contain any text/SVG/image children and the surrounding tree is static.\n\n**Why:** Timeline-driven rotation only moves the motion-bound subtree's SDF primitives (patched in place by `apply_binding_deltas`). The cached text positions are still valid as long as nothing in the rotating subtree is text — which is the spinner case.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Use `is_any_position_animating()` (new sibling on `MotionBindings`) instead of `is_any_animating()` when deciding text/SVG/image cache reuse. It's identical to `is_any_animating` except it excludes `rotation_timeline`.\n- Spring rotation (`b.rotation`) is still counted — those rotations are typically on UI elements with labels / decorations where stale glyph positions would visibly drift mid-animation.\n- If a future widget uses `rotation_timeline` on a subtree that *does* contain text/SVG, this heuristic will leave the text frozen. Today only `cn::spinner` does that. Revisit when adding the second such widget.\n\nSee also [[gotcha-canvas-fast-path-freeze]] (canvas case for the same cache_hit gate) and the Compositor v2 plan in `~/.claude/plans/purring-juggling-tulip.md` (Phase 3 replaces this whole cache_hit dance with per-region dispatch).","files":null}]}